-- title:
--   Continuity of the w-series in the evaluation point
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative ring, $p$ a prime, $d$ a natural number, and let $a : \mathbb{N} \to \mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\ d)\ \mathcal{O}$ be a sequence of power series in $d$ variables each of whose constant coefficients vanishes. Let $g$ be a commutative $\mathcal{O}$-algebra in which $(p : g)$ is a non-zero-divisor and which is adically complete for $J = \mathrm{span}\{(p:g)\}$. Let $x, x' : \mathrm{Fin}\ d \to g$ have all coordinates in the radical of $J$, let $r \ge 1$, and suppose $x_j - x'_j \in \mathrm{span}\{(p:g)^r\}$ for every $j$. Writing $u_n = \mathrm{adicEval}\ J\ x\ (a_n)$ and $u'_n = \mathrm{adicEval}\ J\ x'\ (a_n)$ for the $J$-adic evaluations of $a_n$ at $x$, resp. $x'$ (i.e. `MvPowerSeries.eval₂` of $a_n$ along $\mathcal{O} \to g$), the conclusion is that $$\mathrm{wSeries}\ p\ u - \mathrm{wSeries}\ p\ u' \in \mathrm{powSub}\ p\ g\ r,$$ where $\mathrm{powSub}\ p\ g\ r$ is the $g$-submodule of $\mathrm{Localization.Away}\ (p:g)$ generated by the image of $(p:g)^r$, and $\mathrm{wSeries}\ p\ b$ is a chosen $p$-adic limit, in the sense of the filtration by the submodules $\mathrm{powSub}\ p\ g\ s$, of the partial sums $\sum_{n < N} \mathrm{invPow}\ p\ g\ n \cdot (b_n^{p^n})$ when such a limit exists, and $0$ otherwise.
--
--   This is the statement that Fontaine's $w$-series depends on the evaluation point with no loss of $p$-adic precision: a congruence $x \equiv x' \bmod p^r$ in the coordinates propagates to the same precision $p^r$ for the resulting element of the localisation away from $p$. It supplies the uniqueness half of the Newton-type iteration in [`Deformation.FontaineLift.existsUnique_sub_mem_and_wSeries_adicEval_eq_of_isUnit_linearPart`](thm.html#Deformation.FontaineLift.existsUnique_sub_mem_and_wSeries_adicEval_eq_of_isUnit_linearPart).
